{"lecture_id":"2026-08-06-M6-2","lecture_summary":"The lecture develops wave-optics problem solving across double-slit interference, diffraction gratings, spectroscopy, and single-slit diffraction. Its main moves are choosing the correct fringe condition, connecting angle to screen position, deciding between exact trigonometry and a small-angle approximation, enforcing physical order limits, and distinguishing grating bright maxima from single-slit dark minima.","videos":[{"rank":1,"title":"Young's Double Slit Experiment","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xaAthgG0o8o","reason":"Establishes the prerequisite interference picture, slit–screen geometry, bright-fringe spacing, and constructive versus destructive interference used throughout the lecture."},{"rank":2,"title":"Diffraction Grating Problems - Physics","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gf7j2fumz70","reason":"Directly covers the grating equation and calculations involving fringe order, diffraction angle, wavelength, and line density—the skills needed for the lecture’s lines-per-millimeter and allowable-order examples."},{"rank":3,"title":"Single Slit Diffraction - Physics Problems","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9hCrhllI0ck","reason":"Covers single-slit calculations using slit width, wavelength, and screen distance, including the angular and linear width of the central maximum; it reinforces the shift from locating bright grating fringes to analyzing single-slit minima."}],"coverage_gaps":["No strong playlist match covers spectroscopy: wavelength separation, atomic absorption and emission fingerprints, stellar absorption lines, or inferring astronomical composition.","No strong match covers the lecture’s treatment of secondary single-slit maxima, including the midpoint approximation, the sinc-squared intensity law, and the exact condition tan(β)=β.","The playlist descriptions do not confirm coverage of the lecture’s full exact-versus-small-angle comparison or the derivation and symmetric counting of the maximum physically allowed grating orders."]}
